---
title: Turdidae
---
# Turdidae

Turdidae is the thrush family, medium-sized songbirds with a strong musical
voice and a broadly omnivorous diet. They feed on worms, insects and fruit, and
take much of their food by hopping on open ground and pausing to watch and
listen. The song is loud, fluting and delivered from an exposed perch, and in
several species it is among the most complex produced by any bird. Most build a
cup nest of grass wedged into a fork and supported from below. See
[[common-blackbird]] and [[european-robin]].
